Key assertions validated:
- test_the_bound_replaces_the_calling_shell: uses ${BASHPID:-$(exec /bin/sh ...)} to get true pid, not $$
- test_an_owner_that_dies_during_startup_ends_the_command: watchdog uses absolute /bin/sh, pid non-empty numeric, terminates after owner death
- test_owner_detection_swaps_to_ppid_when_bashpid_absent: verifies swap logic on both bash versions

Demonstrating absolute /bin/sh fallback still works when PATH lacks sh:
PATH=/tmp/empty-path-test owner=26865 self=26865
